This repository contains code adapted from other projects, prompt texts reproduced from published papers and
software, and reimplementations of published methods. Each is listed below with its source and license; the license
texts that travel with copied code are in licenses/.

Third-party code adapted here
- A-mem-sys (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 AGI Research; licenses/A-mem-sys.LICENSE): the note-construction and
  memory-evolution prompts in src/flexamem/memory/prompts.py (verbatim; their output schemas adapted for strict
  structured output), and the evolution step amem_evolve in src/flexamem/memory/linker.py (adapted, with repairs).
- mini-swe-agent 2.3.0 (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Kilian A. Lieret and Carlos E. Jimenez;
  licenses/mini-swe-agent.LICENSE.md): parts of src/flexamem/adapters/mswea.py and src/flexamem/llm/agent_model.py
  (the agent's query and action steps, tool-call parsing) and the observation and format-error templates in
  src/flexamem/bench/appworld/runner.py (adapted).
- AppWorld 0.1.3.post1 (Apache License 2.0; licenses/AppWorld.LICENSE): the agent instructions in
  src/flexamem/bench/appworld/runner.py are a condensed and modified version of AppWorld's ReAct agent prompt, without
  its few-shot demonstration.
- OpenHands (MIT License outside its enterprise/ directory, licenses/OpenHands.LICENSE, as distributed with
  openhands-ai 1.11.0; https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands; Xingyao Wang et al., ICLR 2025,
  arXiv:2407.16741; OpenHands Agent SDK, MLSys 2026, arXiv:2511.03690): the summarizing-condenser prompt in
  src/flexamem/memory/prompts.py (verbatim), as used in MemGym (Wujiang Xu et al., arXiv:2605.20833), for the
  Summary+A-MEM baseline.

Prompt texts reproduced from published papers
These are short instructions, included with attribution so that the reported results can be reproduced. They are not
covered by this repository's MIT License; any copyright in them remains with their authors.
- LongMemEval (Di Wu et al., ICLR 2025, arXiv:2410.10813): reader and answer-checking prompts, transcribed from the
  paper and its evaluation script (src/flexamem/bench/longmemeval/).
- Mem0 (Prateek Chhikara et al., ECAI 2025, arXiv:2504.19413): the LoCoMo answer prompt and LLM-as-a-judge prompt
  (src/flexamem/bench/locomo/prompts.py).
- ReadAgent, MemGAS and Sculptor (below): their prompts are reproduced from the papers where the papers print them and
  adapted where src/flexamem/memory/prompts.py says so.

Methods reimplemented from the papers (no code from the authors' repositories)
- ReadAgent (Kuang-Huei Lee et al., ICML 2024, arXiv:2402.09727): src/flexamem/methods/readagent.py
- MemGAS (Derong Xu et al., ICLR 2026, arXiv:2505.19549): src/flexamem/methods/memgas.py
- Sculptor (Mo Li et al., ICLR 2026, arXiv:2508.04664): src/flexamem/methods/sculptor.py
- Adaptive Focus Memory (Christopher Cruz, 2025, arXiv:2511.12712, preprint): src/flexamem/methods/afm.py. The paper
  prints no prompts; ours are written from its description.
- Observation masking (Tobias Lindenbauer et al., "The Complexity Trap", NeurIPS 2025 DL4C workshop,
  arXiv:2508.21433): src/flexamem/adapters/mswea.py

Benchmarks and software used but not redistributed (downloaded or installed separately, under their own terms)
- LongMemEval-S, cleaned release (Hugging Face xiaowu0162/longmemeval-cleaned).
- LoCoMo (Adyasha Maharana et al., ACL 2024, arXiv:2402.17753; snap-research/locomo).
- SWE-bench (Carlos E. Jimenez et al., ICLR 2024, arXiv:2310.06770), SWE-bench Verified, and the swebench 4.1.0
  harness (MIT License).
- AppWorld (Harsh Trivedi et al., ACL 2024, arXiv:2407.18901), appworld 0.1.3.post1 (Apache License 2.0).
- sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (embeddings), tiktoken o200k_base (token counting), litellm and openai
  (API clients).
